The hyperpigmentation treatment market encompasses products and procedures designed to reduce dark patches, uneven skin tone, and excess pigmentation caused by sun exposure, hormonal changes, aging, and post-inflammatory responses. Demand is increasing as consumers place greater emphasis on skincare and seek effective solutions for conditions such as melasma, post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation, and solar lentigines.

Treatment options range from topical creams and serums to professional chemical peels, laser procedures, and other dermatological interventions. Greater access to specialist skin clinics and the growing availability of skincare products through retail and online channels are also contributing to market development.

